3. Third-party assets keep their own licenses:

- MultiBLiMP 1.0, Jumelet et al., 2025: the unchanged Romanian data is
  CC-BY-4.0. Full attribution is in data/README.md. Its Apache-2.0 code is
  not included.
- GPT-BERT, Charpentier and Samuel, 2024: the original implementation is
  MIT licensed at https://github.com/ltgoslo/gpt-bert. Its copyright notice
  is preserved in code/vendor/gpt_bert/LICENSE.
  Our runs also use https://github.com/babylm-org/multilingual-training.
  That implementation and converter are not bundled because we have not
  confirmed a license for those modifications. Obtain the pinned checkout
  separately as described in code/README.md. The original GPT-BERT license
  does not assign a license to those modifications.
- BabyBabelLM Romanian, Jumelet et al., 2026: not included. The Hugging Face
  dataset is gated and lists an unknown aggregate license, with licensing
  metadata for individual documents. Obtain it from the source linked in
  code/README.md.
- YouTube captions: not included. Creators retain rights over caption text.
  The manifests contain identifiers, metadata and hashes. Rehydration is
  subject to platform terms and availability.
